The distribution obligation is the repository's `NOTICE`, which `vite.config.ts`
copies into `dist/index.html`: that bundle is committed and embedded in the
binary, so it ships elkjs in object form.

The dependency is confined to this directory. `layout.ts` states the contract
with no reference to elkjs, and `operatorView.ts` takes a `GraphLayout` rather
than constructing one, so `elk.ts` is imported once outside this directory —
where `main.ts` mounts the pane. Replacing the engine replaces `elk.ts` and that
one import.
